From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:59:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Move to the end of the media resource at the end of
 the stream

The media engine can signal the end of the stream before it reports a
playback position at the end of the media resource, for example for short
resources. The element then fired `ended` without `pause`, and stayed
unpaused with `ended` false. Move the current playback position to the end
of the media resource first, like other browsers do, so that the steps for
reaching the end pause the element. Likewise, move it to the earliest
possible position when the stream ends while playing backwards.

video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html now times out instead of
failing. With the timeout multiplier of CI, its check that the video
did not play yet runs after the 3 s video ended, and now finds it
paused. It then waits for a play event that never comes, as Servo
doesn't defer the load of lazy videos.

Fork note: meant for upstream, together with the next patch, which
depends on it: without this change, elements that end playback with the
position short of the end stay unpaused, and the next patch would keep
them alive until their document goes away. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: played-loop.html passes now, and the expectation of
video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html is updated.

Validation: Release builds of upstream f040186a7ee: played-loop.html passes with this change and fails without it in every run; `<audio>` with sound_0 and `<video>` with test-1s now end with `pause` before `ended` and with `currentTime == duration` (before, `ended` fired with `paused` false); a `<video>` played backwards from 1 s now ends at 0 (without the backwards part of this change, at 0.007 s in some runs). The whole series on that base against the same build without it, `./mach test-wpt --processes 4` of html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements, the-video-element, the-audio-element, infrastructure/assumptions/allowed-to-play.html, webaudio/the-audio-api/the-mediaelementaudiosourcenode-interface and 2 _mozilla media tests (460 tests): see the next two patches. video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html, in a CI run of this branch and locally with `--timeout-multiplier 2` as CI runs it: TIMEOUT with this change in every run (2 alone, 3 in parallel with the media tests at `--processes 16`), FAIL without it (2 runs); without the multiplier, FAIL either way.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; root-caused, written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .../html/embedded_content/htmlmediaelement.rs  | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 .../media-elements/played-loop.html.ini        |  3 ---
 ...loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html.ini |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/played-loop.html.ini

diff --git a/components/script/dom/html/embedded_content/htmlmediaelement.rs b/components/script/dom/html/embedded_content/htmlmediaelement.rs
index 9266f37f2f5..fefeac2c16b 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/html/embedded_content/htmlmediaelement.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/html/embedded_content/htmlmediaelement.rs
@@ -2441,9 +2441,23 @@ impl HTMLMediaElement {
             return;
         }
 
+        // The media engine can signal the end of the stream before it reports a position at the
+        // end of the media resource in the direction of playback.
         match self.direction_of_playback() {
-            PlaybackDirection::Forwards => self.end_of_playback_in_forwards_direction(cx),
-            PlaybackDirection::Backwards => self.end_of_playback_in_backwards_direction(),
+            PlaybackDirection::Forwards => {
+                let duration = self.duration.get();
+                if duration.is_finite() && self.current_playback_position.get() < duration {
+                    self.playback_position_changed(cx, duration);
+                }
+                self.end_of_playback_in_forwards_direction(cx)
+            },
+            PlaybackDirection::Backwards => {
+                let earliest_possible_position = self.earliest_possible_position();
+                if self.current_playback_position.get() > earliest_possible_position {
+                    self.playback_position_changed(cx, earliest_possible_position);
+                }
+                self.end_of_playback_in_backwards_direction()
+            },
         }
     }
 
diff --git a/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/played-loop.html.ini b/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/played-loop.html.ini
deleted file mode 100644
index d2ae9fd373f..00000000000
--- a/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/played-loop.html.ini
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,3 +0,0 @@
-[played-loop.html]
-  [played TimeRanges should be preserved and not reset when video loops]
-    expected: FAIL
diff --git a/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html.ini b/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html.ini
index c3daf0f98b4..3a3b6300762 100644
--- a/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html.ini
+++ b/tests/wpt/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html.ini
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
 [video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html]
   expected: ERROR
   [Video with loading=lazy and autoplay does not play while not visible, then plays once scrolled into view]
-    expected: FAIL
+    expected: TIMEOUT
